+## Beerten validation, 2026-09-11 (batch 6)
+
+The [batch-6 report](../outputs/beerten_validation_batch6_20260911/REPORT.md)
+supersedes the unexecuted status above only for Beerten. The unmodified
+MatACDC 1.0 `case5_stagg` / `case5_stagg_MTDCslack` example was executed and
+compared with its manual and a separate Python implementation. It differs
+from the 2010 paper and the local case: published P/Q controls are at the PCC,
+while the project case sets internal converter powers. The 2010 article lacks
+a complete numerical station/DC input table; its full PF is not claimed
+reproduced from exact inputs.
+
+The separately named `beerten_constant_pq_capability_batch6` scenario retains
+the saved loading direction and original equipment data. Its available
+capability enforcement was exercised, including generator/converter mode
+transitions and CPF step sensitivity. Slack exemptions, unavailable limits,
+base feasibility conflicts under generic capability assumptions and
+termination diagnostics prevent an equipment-compliant margin claim.
+Published PF agreement does not validate this project's CPF margin.
+IEEE/Nordic/CIGRE conversions remain unexecuted in this batch.
