+## Beerten capability and reference validation (batch 6)
+
+`t_beerten_reporting_batch6(0)` checks solved public unified-PF tables,
+including generator reordering and offline rows. `t_beerten_capability_batch6`
+checks genuine generator/VSC capability transitions, every accepted point's
+full electrical equations and fresh effective tap/shunt decision, unchanged
+ratings/loading, and CPF step sensitivity:
+
+```matlab
+t_beerten_capability_batch6(0, fullfile(pwd,'outputs','beerten_capability_new_run'));
+```
+
+The post-capability handoff re-solves existing voltage controls and then
+rechecks capability. It introduces no freeze, rating or tolerance changes.
+The test explicitly retains the slack's generic-curve conflict; it does not
+certify all-equipment feasibility. Independent Python PF and archived MatACDC
+validation are separate from this internal gate. See the
+[batch-6 report](../outputs/beerten_validation_batch6_20260911/REPORT.md).
